  "answer": "I'll start by reading the debugging skill and locating how special prices are applied on the storefront API.The discount is dropped in two places: the admin mapper stores the end date in the start-date field, and the price calculator then requires the start date to be both before and after today. I'll add tests that fail on that, then fix both.Special prices that include an end date were ignored in two places. When a product was created through the admin API, `PersistableProductAvailabilityMapper` stored the discount end date in the start-date field, and `ProductPriceUtils.finalPrice` then required that start date to be both before and after today, so an active special was never applied. The end date is now stored on the end-date field, and the price calculator treats a special as active when the start date is in the past and the end date is still in the future. An end date alone, or no dates at all, still applies the discount as before.\n\nVERIFICATION: {\"ran\": [\"mvn -pl sm-core,sm-shop -am test -Dtest=ProductPriceUtilsDiscountTest,PersistableProductAvailabilityMapperTest -DfailIfNoTests=false\"], \"result\": \"passed\", \"could_not_verify\": [\"full Shopizer test suite\", \"live admin create then storefront product response\"], \"missing\": [\"a documented end-to-end fixture that creates a product with a special end date and reads the storefront price\"]}",
